{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266489,"nonce":"fD11QwvwGQFQVYlpJWCeWAL7ob4=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis), story-level: saved views and flows are still one thing, and the last piece of the earlier model goes away — a flow does not return a render spec, it calls a view. A view (`work.view.board`, `work.view.list`, `work.view.gantt`) is an atomic capability of git-work: the call renders, handles interaction, writes its own edits through the host and blocks on the script's thread until the user quits. `items` may be a provider function so the view refreshes itself from the ref watcher, and the return value is the user's answer — a list with `pick=True` gives back the chosen item, which `flow pick` (9a24c8e) needs. The spec survives only as the headless serialization for agents, `--gui` and the gui process; the code in package `view` and `git work view` is that backend and the interim behaviour until the terminal renderer (84dfbde) lands. Callbacks are sketched and deferred, not decided. Affects f37603c (a saved view calls a view), 52a2797 (the command and package are the headless backend), 84dfbde (the blocking terminal backend) and 8b06191 (the HTML backend). Design: doc/design/config-entity.md E9, doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}